cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Predictive Maintenance for Autonomous Delivery Robots: Reference Architecture and Pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zagaia
    given-names: Luca
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucazagaia/Predictive-Maintenance"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end implementation of the predictive-maintenance architecture designed in a
  TU Berlin bachelor's thesis for autonomous last-mile delivery robots: edge anomaly
  detection, cloud remaining-useful-life estimation and a decision layer that fuses both
  into one maintenance recommendation, connected by typed messages over named topics.
  MVT-Flow (voraus-AD) and the Li et al. 1-D CNN (NASA C-MAPSS) serve as reference models.
keywords:
  - predictive maintenance
  - reference architecture
  - edge computing
  - anomaly detection
  - remaining useful life
  - normalizing flows
  - autonomous delivery robots
  - pytorch
